      "id": "phrase-ya-esta",
      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "ya está",
      "answerEn": "Ya está can mean “that's it,” “it's done,” or “all set.”",
      "noteEn": "This is an everyday fixed expression. It tells the listener that something is complete or that nothing else needs to be added. The most natural English wording depends on the situation.",
      "tags": [
        "A2",
        "conversation",
        "common expression"
      ],
      "questionEn": "What can ya está mean when something is finished?",
      "example": {
        "es": "Ya está. Podemos irnos.",
        "en": "That's it. We can leave."
      },
